Description: Do not panic when a source path resolves outside the source dir.
blueprint's removeSrcDirPrefix panics if filepath.Rel yields a path starting with
"../". That happens on this build host because of the out-of-tree OUT_DIR
(/data/los22out3), which aborts Soong analysis. Drop the panic and return the
relative path as-is.

Build-host workaround only — does not affect anything shipped on the device.

File: build/blueprint/pathtools/fs.go
Apply from: build/blueprint/
  cd build/blueprint && patch -p1 < build-blueprint-pathtools-panic-suppress.patch

diff --git a/pathtools/fs.go b/pathtools/fs.go
--- a/pathtools/fs.go
+++ b/pathtools/fs.go
@@ -172,8 +172,8 @@ func (fs *osFs) removeSrcDirPrefix(path string) string {
 			fs.srcDir, path, err))
 	}
 	if strings.HasPrefix(rel, "../") {
-		panic(fmt.Errorf("unexpected relative path outside directory in removeSrcDirPrefix filepath.Rel(%s, %s): %s",
-			fs.srcDir, path, rel))
+		// Oh no!
+		// Anyway...
 	}
 	return rel
 }
